"title": "R9410 ff.&nbsp;246&ndash;247, Latin: &ldquo;nos cum adversario nostro pacem non habere&rdquo;",
"caption": "Three lines of the Latin letter of 30 June 1534 (ff. 246&ndash;247), sign by sign, with the values of the System A&prime; key as re-learned for this letter and the hand reading aligned to the signs. The hourglass sign is the code for <i>Dominationes</i>, as F.G. is in the German letters; the bar marks the end of a manuscript line. Signs marked uncertain take a value the rest of the letter does not confirm; the one sign marked ? after nostro is passed over by the reading.",
"unit": "signs",
"key_note": "Homophonic substitution of invented signs, Greek-looking letters and numerals, written without word division; the key is the improved R9407 (Augurelio) key carried over by sign shape and re-learned on this letter. Word division is editorial.",
